------------------- Class-Related Keywords -----------------------

   class      : Used to define a class.
   interface  : Used to define an interface.
   extends    : Indicates that a class inherits from a superclass.
   implements : Used for a class to implement an interface.
   new        : Used to create a new object.
   abstract   : Used to define abstract classes and methods.
   final      : Used to mark a class, method, or variable as unchangeable (non-extendable).
   static     : Used to declare a member that belongs to the class, rather than an instance.
   void       : Specifies that a method does not return a value.



-------------------- Access Modifiers ---------------------

   public    : Makes a class, method, or variable accessible from anywhere.
   private   : Restricts access to within the same class.
   protected : Allows access within the same package or subclasses.
   default (no modifier): Accessible within the same package.



------------------ Exception Handling Keywords -----------------------------

  try     : Used to start a block of code that might throw an exception.
  catch   : Used to handle exceptions thrown by the try block.
  finally : A block that always executes after the try block, regardless of whether an exception was thrown.
  throw   : Used to explicitly throw an exception.
  throws  : Declares an exception that might be thrown by a method.



---------------- Object-Oriented Keywords ( OOPS ) ---------------------------

   this       : Refers to the current object instance.
   super      : Refers to the parent class object.
   instanceof : Checks if an object is an instance of a specified class or interface.







